{
  "name": "imported-mesh-prism",
  "reference": "Benchmark J1 (imported triangle-mesh geometry, #350). An ASCII STL of a regular 32-gon prism of circumradius 1 and height 2 file units, imported with geometry.import at unitLength 1 mm and welded into a solid by the geometry kernel. Its volume and surface area have closed forms that owe nothing to the importer: a regular n-gon of circumradius R has area (n/2) R^2 sin(2 pi / n), so the prism holds (n/2) R^2 sin(2 pi/n) h = 6.2428903045 mm^3, and its side is n chords of 2 R sin(pi/n) by h, giving a total surface of 18.7890842667 mm^2. The mesh is exactly the polyhedron, so both are matched to 1e-12 relative, not approached. The face patches found by flood-filling across edges sharper than 30 degrees are the 32 side facets plus the two caps, and a geometry.nameFace plane rule on the top cap resolves on the lattice mesh, which is how an imported face is named durably. Analytic volume from the same formula for a cube (side 1 file unit) is checked by the engine tests; this case is the Command-level form.",
